From 819867267be1a4565c19bd975000017453252aef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lwb6 <lwb.6@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:49:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix: bring the artifact reader and platform layer onto
 Windows

Read artifacts with CreateFileW and serve the payload through MapViewOfFile plus
ReadFile/GetOverlappedResult on a FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED handle, replacing the POSIX open/mmap/pread
path. The direct read treats ERROR_HANDLE_EOF and short transfers as end of data, shares the file
with concurrent writers so a reader never fails against an in-progress download, and renders paths
as UTF-8 for diagnostics instead of the ANSI code page.

Use the CRT's Windows spellings at the remaining platform points: _isatty for terminal detection,
localtime_s for the service log timestamp, _getpid for the server instance id, and
GetConsoleScreenBufferInfo for the progress width.

Two MSVC linkage fixes preserve Linux behaviour: spell out the defaulted move operations of the plan
types (MSVC does not emit an out-of-line defaulted specialization the defining translation unit
never uses), and include <cstdlib> before the NVTX v3 header that calls _wgetenv.
